@startuml MVC Pane Lifecycle — Current (Broken) vs Correct Flow

title **MVC Pane Lifecycle — Sprint 0 Task B5**\nView (otmux) must notify Controller (hiveMind) on pane mutations\nModel (claudeCode) is unaffected — sessions are bound to TTYs, not pane indices

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam participantPadding 20
skinparam boxPadding 10

actor Tron
participant "otmux\n(View)" as V #LightBlue
participant "hiveMind\n(Controller)" as C #LightGreen
participant "claudeCode\n(Model)" as M #LightYellow
database "roles.env\n(Registry)" as R #LightGray

== CURRENT FLOW — BROKEN ==

note over V,C #FFcccc
  **Pane operations do NOT notify Controller.**
  Registry keeps stale pane→role mappings.
  hiveMind.resolve returns wrong targets.
end note

Tron -> V : otmux split.h ooshTeam:0.0
activate V
V -> V : tmux split-window -h\n(new pane inserted at 0.1)
note right of V #FFcccc
  **tmux renumbers ALL panes:**
  0.0 stays
  NEW → 0.1 (empty zsh)
  old 0.1 → 0.2 (expert)
  old 0.2 → 0.3 (tester)
  old 0.3 → 0.4 (expert-shell)
  old 0.4 → 0.5 (tester-shell)
end note
deactivate V

note over R #FFcccc
  **Registry (STALE):**
  ooshTeam:0.1 | oosh-expert ← WRONG (now empty zsh)
  ooshTeam:0.2 | oosh-tester ← WRONG (now expert)
end note

Tron -> C : hiveMind resolve oosh-expert
activate C
C -> R : grep "oosh-expert"
R --> C : ooshTeam:0.1
C --> Tron : ooshTeam:0.1 ← **WRONG** (expert is at 0.2 now)
deactivate C

|||

Tron -> V : otmux pane.swap 0.1 0.2
activate V
V -> V : tmux swap-pane -s 0.1 -t 0.2
deactivate V
note over R #FFcccc
  **THREE things broken after swap:**
  1. Registry unchanged → resolve returns wrong pane
  2. Pane titles unchanged → visual labels lie
  3. HIVEMIND_ROLE env unchanged →
     sender prefix shows wrong identity
     ([@PO-shell] instead of [@scrum-master])
end note

== CORRECT FLOW — FIXED (Task B5) ==

note over V,C #ccFFcc
  **Pane operations notify Controller via protected methods.**
  Registry stays consistent. resolve returns correct targets.
end note

Tron -> V : otmux split.h ooshTeam:0.0
activate V
V -> V : tmux split-window -h\n(pane indices shift)
V -> C : **hiveMind protected.panes.shifted**\n(session, old→new index map)
activate C
C -> R : update all entries for session:\n0.1→0.2, 0.2→0.3, 0.3→0.4, 0.4→0.5
deactivate C
deactivate V

note over R #ccFFcc
  **Registry (CORRECT):**
  ooshTeam:0.2 | oosh-expert ✓
  ooshTeam:0.3 | oosh-tester ✓
end note

Tron -> C : hiveMind resolve oosh-expert
activate C
C -> R : grep "oosh-expert"
R --> C : ooshTeam:0.2
C --> Tron : ooshTeam:0.2 ← **CORRECT**
deactivate C

|||

Tron -> V : otmux pane.swap 0.1 0.2
activate V
V -> V : tmux swap-pane
V -> C : **hiveMind protected.panes.swapped**\n(session, paneA, paneB)
activate C
C -> R : 1. swap registry entries:\n0.1↔0.2 roles exchanged
C -> V : 2. swap pane titles:\notmux pane.title 0.1 <roleB>\notmux pane.title 0.2 <roleA>
C -> V : 3. swap HIVEMIND_ROLE env:\notmux send.enter 0.1 "export HIVEMIND_ROLE=<roleB>"\notmux send.enter 0.2 "export HIVEMIND_ROLE=<roleA>"
note right of C #ccFFcc
  **Three things must update on swap:**
  1. Registry (Controller state)
  2. Pane titles (View labels)
  3. HIVEMIND_ROLE env (Model-in-View)

  Without #3: sender prefix shows
  wrong identity ([@PO-shell] instead
  of [@scrum-master])
end note
deactivate C
deactivate V

|||

Tron -> V : otmux pane.kill ooshTeam:0.3
activate V
V -> V : tmux kill-pane\n(indices shift down)
V -> C : **hiveMind protected.pane.removed**\n(session, removed_index)
activate C
C -> R : remove entry for 0.3\nshift 0.4→0.3, 0.5→0.4
deactivate C
deactivate V

|||

Tron -> V : otmux pane.move ooshTeam:0.2 otherSession
activate V
V -> V : tmux move-pane
V -> C : **hiveMind protected.pane.moved**\n(from_session:pane, to_session:pane)
activate C
C -> R : remove from source session\nadd to target session
deactivate C
deactivate V

== MODEL LAYER — UNAFFECTED ==

note over M #LightYellow
  **claudeCode sessions are bound to TTYs, not pane indices.**
  When panes split/swap/move, the Claude process stays on its TTY.
  The TTY→pane mapping changes (tmux renumbers), but the process doesn't move.

  claudeCode.session.id uses: ps args → sessions.env → JSONL
  None of these reference pane indices — they use TTY or UUID.

  **Model is portable. Only View↔Controller binding needs fixing.**
end note

== PROTECTED METHODS NEEDED (hiveMind) ==

note over C #ccFFcc
  **New hiveMind protected methods for otmux to call:**

  hiveMind.protected.panes.shifted <session>
    — re-scan pane list, remap registry by TTY matching
    — called after: split, kill (any op that renumbers)

  hiveMind.protected.panes.swapped <session> <paneA> <paneB>
    — exchange two registry entries
    — called after: pane.swap

  hiveMind.protected.pane.moved <from> <to>
    — remove from source, add to target session
    — called after: pane.move, pane.join

  **Pattern: same as existing protected.session.renamed (line 2505)**
  **Guard: command -v hiveMind >/dev/null (otmux works without hiveMind)**
end note

== OBSERVER PATTERN — EXISTING PRECEDENT ==

note over V,C #LightBlue
  **Already implemented for session rename (otmux line 183):**

  otmux.rename() calls:
    command -v hiveMind >/dev/null 2>&1 &&
      hiveMind protected.session.renamed "$oldName" "$newName"

  **Same pattern for pane operations:**

  otmux.split.h() should call:
    command -v hiveMind >/dev/null 2>&1 &&
      hiveMind protected.panes.shifted "$session"

  otmux.pane.swap() should call:
    command -v hiveMind >/dev/null 2>&1 &&
      hiveMind protected.panes.swapped "$session" "$paneA" "$paneB"
end note

@enduml
